{"name":"Archaeological Site","hex":"#8e785c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"archaeological","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the science or research of archaeology."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/archaeological"},{"term":"site","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The place where anything is fixed; situation; local position","A place fitted or chosen for any certain permanent use or occupation"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To situate or place a building or construction project."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/site"}],"entries":[{"title":"Archaeological site","blocks":[{"text":"An archaeological site is a place in which evidence of past activity is preserved, and which has been, or may be, investigated using the discipline of archaeology and represents a part of the archaeological record. Sites may range from those with few or no remains visible above ground, to buildings and other structures still in use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/LYablonskyFilipovkaKurganR1.jpg/330px-LYablonskyFilipovkaKurganR1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeological_site"},{"title":"Archaeology","blocks":[{"text":"Archaeology or archeology is the study of human activity through the recovery and analysis of material culture. The archaeological record consists of artifacts, architecture, biofacts or ecofacts, sites, and cultural landscapes. Archaeology can be considered both a social science and a branch of the humanities. It is usually considered an independent academic discipline, but may also be classified as part of anthropology, history or geography. The discipline involves surveying, excavation, and eventually analysis of data collected, to learn more about the past. In broad scope, archaeology relies on cross-disciplinary research."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Dolina-Pano-3_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Dolina-Pano-3_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeology"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg/250px-Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg/330px-Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg/250px-Dion_archaeological_site_107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADion_archaeological_site_107.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg/250px-Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg/330px-Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg/250px-Archaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArchaeological_Site_of_Cyrene-109022.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Archaeological_Site_of_Sabratha-108975.jpg/250px-Archaeological_Site_of_Sabratha-108975.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm